// Logos project — https://github.com/victor-smirnov/logos
//
// el.peg — the EL (Expression Language) grammar for peg_gen_logos, in
// SCHEMA-EMISSION mode (ADR 0012 peg-frontend, §6). It specifies construction
// of the EXISTING WQL scalar/relational IR (SExpr / RExpr, `logos.std.wql.ir`)
// as first-class Writ schema views — `doc.make::<S>()` + typed schema field
// writes + `WRef<S>` edges — dogfooding ADR 0011. It is the peg-generated
// replacement for the hand-written recursive-descent `ElParser` in
// `stdlib/std/wql/el.logos`.
//
// The grammar is a FAITHFUL transcription of the EL grammar documented in
// el.logos:9-21 (the CEL-precedence expression chain + the one comprehension
// form):
//
//   expr     := ternary
//   ternary  := or ( '?' expr ':' expr )?            // CEL conditional  → SCond
//   or       := and ( '||' and )*                    // → SBin(OP_OR)
//   and      := equality ( '&&' equality )*          // → SBin(OP_AND)
//   equality := compare ( ('=='|'!=') compare )*     // → SBin(OP_EQ/OP_NE)
//   compare  := add ( ('<='|'>='|'<'|'>') add )*     // → SBin(OP_LT..OP_GE)
//   add      := mul ( ('+'|'-') mul )*               // → SBin(OP_ADD/OP_SUB)
//   mul      := unary ( ('*'|'/'|'%') unary )*       // → SBin(OP_MUL/DIV/MOD)
//   unary    := ('!'|'-') unary | postfix            // → SUn(OP_NOT/OP_NEG)
//   postfix  := primary ( '.' ident )*               // field access → SField
//   primary  := int | bool | string | '$' ident | ident ( '(' args ')' )?
//             | '(' expr ')'
//             | '[' expr 'for' ident 'in' postfix ( 'if' expr )? ']'  // SComp
//
// LEFT-ASSOCIATIVITY is expressed with fold-mode `$0` (the fold accumulator =
// the running LHS), matching the demo grammar and logos.peg's `add_expr`. Each
// operator gets its OWN fold sub-alternative so it can stamp the correct CEL
// operator id (SBin.op / SUn.op) as an INT_LIT — the op-id table below mirrors
// el.logos's OP_* constants exactly (CEL canon, stable across backends):
//
//   SBin.op: OR=1 AND=2 EQ=3 NE=4 LT=5 LE=6 GT=7 GE=8 ADD=9 SUB=10 MUL=11 DIV=12 MOD=13
//   SUn.op : NOT=1 NEG=2
//
// ── KNOWN GENERATOR GAPS (resolved in the parser-SWAP phase, NOT here) ──────
// Phase 3 authors this grammar against the schemas AS THEY ARE (mandate: "Do
// NOT change the schemas"). Two schema fields need a generator capability the
// current schema-emission mode does not yet have — a captured TOKEN whose TEXT
// must become a node scalar/value rather than a child-node edge:
//
//   (G1) SField.key : u8   — the field NAME. The hand-written ElParser interns
//        each `.ident` / bare-ident to a dense u8 key and keeps a side table
//        (field_name/param_name/var_name) that the WQL codegen reads back. A
//        generated parser has no such table; the captured IDENT text must land
//        IN the node. Today `emit_schema_field` maps a captured token → a
//        scalar field as `0 as u8` (codegen.logos:2609). The clean resolution
//        (ADR 0012 peg-frontend §5, Option B) is to store the NAME in the node
//        (a `str` field — which the generator DOES support via captured-IDENT →
//        `wstr_as_str`) so codegen reads `f.name` directly and the dense-id
//        side tables are deleted. That is a one-time IR-shape change + codegen
//        rewrite, out of Phase-3 scope. Until then a generated `SField` here
//        carries `key = 0` (placeholder) — a real captured value once the swap
//        lands. Marked below with `// GAP:key`.
//
//   (G2) SLit.val : WAny   — an INTEGER literal's numeric VALUE. A captured
//        INTEGER token yields a WString-ptr (the text), not the int value; the
//        generator has no token→value decode. The demo grammar sidesteps this
//        with `val: 0` (INT_LIT). A STRING literal, by contrast, IS faithfully
//        stored (captured token text → WAny ref to interned WString), and BOOL
//        literals are exact (INT_LIT/BOOL). So INT literals here carry a
//        placeholder value; the swap phase adds a token→value decode (or routes
//        int literals through a dedicated capture). Marked `// GAP:val`.
//
//   (G3) SParam.idx / SVar.idx : i32 — same class as (G1): the `$name` param
//        and the `for v` loop variable are dense ids in side tables today. The
//        swap stores the NAME on the node (`SParam.name`/`SVar.name` str) — same
//        Option-B resolution. Placeholder idx=0 here. Marked `// GAP:idx`.
//
//   (G4) The comprehension SOURCE (`in <ident>`) and the loop-var binding are
//        resolved by the hand parser's prescan (bind `for v` before parsing the
//        head so `v` references become SVar). A PEG grammar parses positionally;
//        the head's references to the loop var parse as SField/SCall and are
//        rebound to SVar at the metacall (a semantic pass), consistent with the
//        seam's "FE emits symbolic names; metacall resolves" contract (ADR
//        0012-impl-seam §5/§6). RScan.src is a dense param idx today → GAP:idx.
//
// None of these gaps block Phase 3 (author + front-end parse). They are the
// name-interning seam the frontend-plan flagged, to be closed with the IR
// self-describing refactor when the parse step is actually swapped.

%meta {
    name:      "el"
    version:   "1.0"
    namespace: "logos::wql::el"
    output:    "el_parser"
    package:   "logos.std.wql.el_parser"
    prefix:    "El"
}

// The EL entry rule: a full expression → an SExpr root edge handle.
%export { expr }

// ── SCHEMA-EMISSION binding ────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Each `S { field: "type", ... }` names a grammar node (`=> { CODE: "S", ... }`)
// built as the schema `S` (code = `S::CODE`) with typed field writes. Types MUST
// match the field types in ir.logos exactly so the emitted write is correct:
//   "ref T"  → WRef::<T>::from_any(hand_any(<capture>))   (graph edge)
//   "WAny"   → verbatim dynamic value (literal or captured handle)
//   "str"    → interned string field (captured IDENT / STR_LIT)
//   scalar   → <INT_LIT/BOOL> as <type>
// `arena: external` makes the generated `parse_expr(src, doc: &Writ) -> WAny`
// take the caller's Writ arena (the wql!/trama! handler passes its own `h`).
// `ref_wrap: "WRef"` is the ir.logos edge wrapper (also the default).
%schema {
    use:      "logos.std.wql.ir"
    arena:    external
    ref_wrap: "WRef"

    // Scalar tier — SExpr (ir.logos). SELF-DESCRIBING IR (Option B): leaf nodes
    // carry NAMES as `str` fields, populated from the captured IDENT token — the
    // generator DOES support captured-token → `str` field (`wstr_as_str`). This
    // closes the former GAP:key/GAP:idx: `SField.name`/`SParam.name`/`SCall.fn_name`
    // hold the real identifier text now.
    SLit   { val: "WAny" }                                   // GAP:val for INT still (STRING/BOOL exact); int-value decode TBD
    SParam { name: "str" }                                   // $name — captured IDENT
    SVar   { name: "str" }                                   // loop var — captured IDENT
    SField { base: "ref SExpr", name: "str" }                // field NAME — captured IDENT
    SBin   { op: "i32", lhs: "ref SExpr", rhs: "ref SExpr" }
    SUn    { op: "i32", arg: "ref SExpr" }
    SCall  { fn_name: "str", args: "ref SExprArr" }          // call NAME — captured IDENT
    SCond  { c: "ref SExpr", t: "ref SExpr", e: "ref SExpr" }
    SComp  { plan: "ref RExpr", head: "ref SExpr", var: "str" }

    // Relational tier — RExpr (ir.logos). The comprehension lowers to a scan
    // (+ optional filter) plan; the source is a captured IDENT name.
    RScan   { node_code: "i56", src_name: "str" }            // source NAME — captured IDENT
    RFilter { input: "ref RExpr", pred: "ref SExpr" }
}

// ── Tokens ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
%tokens {
    // Two-char operators FIRST (PEG first-match; the lexer is longest-literal by
    // convention, but keep them ahead for clarity).
    OROR     = "||"
    ANDAND   = "&&"
    EQEQ     = "=="
    NE       = "!="
    LE       = "<="
    GE       = ">="

    // One-char operators / punctuation.
    QUESTION = "?"
    COLON    = ":"
    LT       = "<"
    GT       = ">"
    PLUS     = "+"
    MINUS    = "-"
    STAR     = "*"
    SLASH    = "/"
    PERCENT  = "%"
    BANG     = "!"
    DOT      = "."
    COMMA    = ","
    LPAREN   = "("
    RPAREN   = ")"
    LBRACKET = "["
    RBRACKET = "]"
    DOLLAR   = "$"

    // Keywords (matched as literals; IDENT must come AFTER so `for`/`in`/`if`/
    // `true`/`false` win — PEG orders alternatives, and keyword-vs-ident is
    // resolved at the rule level via ordered choice, so declare them as tokens).
    KW_FOR   = "for"
    KW_IN    = "in"
    KW_IF    = "if"
    TRUE     = "true"
    FALSE    = "false"

    // Literals + identifier.
    INTEGER  = /[0-9]+/
    STRING   = /"([^"\\]|\\.)*"/
    IDENT    = /[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*/

    // Skip whitespace + comments.
    %skip    = /[ \t\r\n]+/
    %skip    = /\/\/[^\n]*/
}

// ── Rules ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
%rules {
    // expr := ternary
    expr <- ternary

    // ternary := or ( '?' expr ':' expr )?    → SCond (CEL conditional)
    // The optional tail folds the condition ($0) into an SCond with then/else.
    ternary <- or ( QUESTION expr COLON expr
                        => { CODE: "SCond", c: $0, t: $2, e: $4 } )?

    // or := and ( '||' and )*                 → SBin(OP_OR = 1)
    or <- and ( OROR and => { CODE: "SBin", op: 1, lhs: $0, rhs: $2 } )*

    // and := equality ( '&&' equality )*      → SBin(OP_AND = 2)
    and <- equality ( ANDAND equality => { CODE: "SBin", op: 2, lhs: $0, rhs: $2 } )*

    // equality := compare ( ('=='|'!=') compare )*   → SBin(OP_EQ=3 / OP_NE=4)
    equality <- compare
                ( EQEQ compare => { CODE: "SBin", op: 3, lhs: $0, rhs: $2 }
                / NE   compare => { CODE: "SBin", op: 4, lhs: $0, rhs: $2 }
                )*

    // compare := add ( ('<='|'>='|'<'|'>') add )*    → SBin(OP_LT=5..OP_GE=8)
    // Two-char ops (<=, >=) are distinct tokens and ordered before <, > anyway.
    compare <- add
               ( LE add => { CODE: "SBin", op: 6, lhs: $0, rhs: $2 }
               / GE add => { CODE: "SBin", op: 8, lhs: $0, rhs: $2 }
               / LT add => { CODE: "SBin", op: 5, lhs: $0, rhs: $2 }
               / GT add => { CODE: "SBin", op: 7, lhs: $0, rhs: $2 }
               )*

    // add := mul ( ('+'|'-') mul )*           → SBin(OP_ADD=9 / OP_SUB=10)
    add <- mul
           ( PLUS  mul => { CODE: "SBin", op: 9,  lhs: $0, rhs: $2 }
           / MINUS mul => { CODE: "SBin", op: 10, lhs: $0, rhs: $2 }
           )*

    // mul := unary ( ('*'|'/'|'%') unary )*   → SBin(OP_MUL=11 / DIV=12 / MOD=13)
    mul <- unary
           ( STAR    unary => { CODE: "SBin", op: 11, lhs: $0, rhs: $2 }
           / SLASH   unary => { CODE: "SBin", op: 12, lhs: $0, rhs: $2 }
           / PERCENT unary => { CODE: "SBin", op: 13, lhs: $0, rhs: $2 }
           )*

    // unary := ('!'|'-') unary | postfix      → SUn(OP_NOT=1 / OP_NEG=2)
    unary <- BANG  unary => { CODE: "SUn", op: 1, arg: $2 }
           / MINUS unary => { CODE: "SUn", op: 2, arg: $2 }
           / postfix

    // postfix := primary ( '.' ident )*       → SField (left-nested edge chain)
    // Each `.ident` step folds the running base ($0) into an SField whose `key`
    // is the field name. GAP:key — the IDENT text ($2) must become the node's
    // field NAME; the current generator stores a placeholder u8 (see header G1).
    postfix <- primary
               ( DOT IDENT => { CODE: "SField", base: $0, name: $2 } )*

    // primary := literals | param | call | var/field-root | paren | comprehension
    //
    // Ordered choice (PEG first-match): keyword literals + comprehension +
    // parenthesised before the bare-identifier field-root fallback.
    primary <- comprehension
             / LPAREN expr RPAREN                     // grouping (value passes through)
             / TRUE    => { CODE: "SLit", val: true }
             / FALSE   => { CODE: "SLit", val: false }
             / STRING  => { CODE: "SLit", val: $1 }   // faithful: interned WString ref
             / INTEGER => { CODE: "SLit", val: 0 }    // GAP:val (int-value decode TBD; see header G2)
             / DOLLAR IDENT => { CODE: "SParam", name: $2 }            // $name — captured IDENT
             / IDENT LPAREN arglist RPAREN => { CODE: "SCall", fn_name: $1, args: $3 }  // call NAME — captured IDENT
             / IDENT   => { CODE: "SField", base: NULLBASE, name: $1 } // bare field-root; captured IDENT
             // Note: a bound comprehension variable also parses as this IDENT
             // field-root and is rebound to SVar at the metacall (header G4).

    // arglist := ( expr ( ',' expr )* )?  →  SExprArr backing (multi-arg call)
    // The SExprArr materialization (fixed-slot fan-out) is built by the WQL
    // handler / a dedicated action; the MVP grammar collects the arg edges with
    // an array capture. GAP: the current schema-emission mode has no SExprArr
    // slot-fill action, so arglist here is a structural placeholder (the handler
    // supplies the SExprArr node). See header note on SCall.
    arglist <- ( expr ( COMMA expr )* )?

    // comprehension := '[' expr 'for' ident 'in' postfix ( 'if' guard )? ']'
    //   →  SComp{ plan = RFilter(RScan(src), guard)? | RScan(src), head = expr }
    // The plan (RScan + optional RFilter) is assembled by the handler from the
    // parsed source + guard; this rule produces the SComp shell with its head +
    // plan edges. GAP:idx — RScan.src is the source ident's dense param id today
    // (header G4). The `for`-var binding is a metacall-time semantic rebind.
    comprehension <- LBRACKET expr KW_FOR IDENT KW_IN postfix comp_guard RBRACKET
                        => { CODE: "SComp", plan: $7, head: $2 }

    // comp_guard := ( 'if' expr )?   → RFilter(scan, expr) or the bare scan.
    // (Placeholder: the scan/filter assembly is handler-side; see comprehension.)
    comp_guard <- ( KW_IF expr )?
}
